# Filing Problem Tracker: settings.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local for local work (`cp .env.example .env.local`). .env.local is ignored by
# git. On a host such as Vercel, enter the same names in the project's environment variable settings.
#
# Every line below is commented out, and the app runs like that: demo mode, made-up sample data, AI off.
# An empty value counts as "not set". src/server/config.ts reads and checks these once at startup and
# stops the server with a plain message when the combination makes no sense.
#
# Only the two NEXT_PUBLIC_ values ever reach the browser. Everything else stays on the server.

# --- Run mode -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set BOTH to run against Supabase (Postgres with row level security, invite-only sign-in).
# Set NEITHER to run in demo mode. Setting only one stops the server at startup.
# Both are built into the browser bundle and the Content-Security-Policy, so rebuild after changing them.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Demo mode ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Signs the demo sign-in cookie. At least 32 characters. Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 48
# Local development works without it (a built-in value is used). A production start in demo mode
# refuses to run unless this is set or ALLOW_DEMO=1.
# DEMO_COOKIE_SECRET=

# 1 confirms that a production start in demo mode (open sign-in, made-up data) is intended.
# ALLOW_DEMO=1

# 1 makes "Reset demo data" also forget every rate limit. Only for a throwaway test server (the
# end-to-end tests set it): left on, any demo account could lift everyone's limits whenever it liked.
# DEMO_RESET_CLEARS_LIMITS=1

# --- AI (optional) --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A Claude API key. With no key every AI feature uses its non-AI fallback and the app is fully usable.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# The model to use. Leave unset to use the default in src/server/config.ts.
# AI_MODEL=

# --- MCP endpoint (optional) ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Demo mode: the bearer token for POST /api/mcp. At least 24 characters. Generate one with:
# openssl rand -hex 32. With no token the endpoint answers 404. Not used in Supabase mode.
# MCP_TOKEN=

# Supabase mode: the project's service role key. It is used for one thing only: looking up a per-user
# MCP token and reading the statistics that token's holder may see (src/server/mcp/supabase-tokens.ts).
# Pages and the rest of the API never use it; they act as the signed-in person. Leave it unset unless
# the MCP endpoint is used: without it the endpoint accepts no token. This key bypasses row level
# security, so treat it as the most sensitive value here and never give it a NEXT_PUBLIC_ name.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Deployment -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The app's own address, for example https://tracker.example.gov. When set, state-changing requests
# must carry exactly this Origin. When unset, the Origin is compared with the request's Host header.
# APP_ORIGIN=

# How many proxies in front of the app append the caller's address to X-Forwarded-For and can be
# believed: 0 (the default) when the app is reached directly, 1 behind one such proxy or on Vercel.
# Sign-in attempts are limited per network address, and the address is taken from that header counting
# this many entries from the right. At 0 the header is not believed at all, because anyone can write
# it, and all sign-in attempts share one limit. Set it too high and the limit can be dodged by sending
# a made-up header.
# TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=0

# --- Rate limits (optional) -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per user, per minute. Defaults: 60 changes, 20 AI requests.
# RATE_LIMIT_MUTATIONS_PER_MINUTE=60
# RATE_LIMIT_AI_PER_MINUTE=20
